  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nOne last afternoon and evening to go as the active pattern of \ndaily shower and storm chances of last week and a half comes to an\nend. Sunday will see a low 10% to 30% chance for isolated showers\nand thunderstorms during the afternoon and evening hours. The \nbest chances to see a storm will again be along a line from Round \nmountain in N Nye county northeast through the Rubies, an into NE \nElko county. Hazard will again be gusty outflow winds up to 50 \nMPH, ground lightning strikes, and brief heavy rainfall. Storm \nmotion will be quick like Saturday so wetting rains are not \nfavored. Monday through next Sunday will see a return of quiet \nSummertime conditions with breezy afternoon winds and very warm \ntemperatures, as the upper ridge continues its slow drift west \neventually setting up over the southern Great Basin and \nstrengthening as it does so. Fire weather, and Heat Risk \nconditions will need to be watched closely as drying out of both \nthe land and atmosphere commences, and overnight relief will be \nshort. Winds will be out of the SW with breezy afternoon winds \nranging at 10 to 20 MPH with gusts up to 30 MPH possible. \nTemperatures will range in the mid 90s to mid 100s. A heat \nadvisory in effect for sections of Elko County for Sunday, and may\nneed to be expanded as heat impacts build through the week. As \nfor Fire weather, RH percent values will drop into the low teens \nto single digits in the afternoons, with overnight recoveries only\nmaking it back to the upper 20s, combined with afternoon winds \nmay lead to periods of elevated to critical fire weather \nconditions. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence for a low chance of a few isolated \nthunderstorms Sunday afternoon. \n\nThere High confidence in the return of quiet Summertime \nconditions, with breezy afternoon winds and very warm temperatures\nMonday through Sunday of next week.",
